      "tag": "3P",
      "h2": "Three Primaries",
      "body_html": "<p>The three primary colours: <strong>rojo</strong> (red), <strong>amarillo</strong> (yellow), <strong>azul</strong> (blue). 'J' sounds like 'h' — say 'ROH-ho'.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "More",
      "h2": "More Colours",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Naranja</strong> (orange), <strong>morado</strong> (purple), <strong>rosa</strong> (pink), <strong>marron</strong> (brown), <strong>gris</strong> (grey).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "BW",
      "h2": "Black & White",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Negro</strong> (black) and <strong>blanco</strong> (white). With feminine nouns they change: <strong>negra</strong>, <strong>blanca</strong>. Most colours follow this -o/-a pattern.</p>"
    }
